{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-souji"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Cleaning Robot Design (Physical AI, Starlink Direct-assisted remote supervision)"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :robotics/cleaning-robot-design
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:household-labor-reduction :disaster-cleanup :accessibility]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :cleaning-robot-design-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:identity :forms :dmn :audit-ledger :robotics :sim]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies [:x402]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :scaffolded
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "R0 scaffold: Cleaning Robot Design Governor ⊣ Advisor actor skeleton.
 Design-only repo: every op is :propose or :observe. There is NO op that
 drives a physical robot — actuator command paths do not exist in this repo
 and must never be added here (physical control belongs to a separate runtime
 repo when one is created). Safety gates (child/pet contact stop, sharp-object
 stop) are permanent structural invariants, inherited from the esim actor's
 SIM-swap-refusal pattern: they are absent from no phase's :auto set and the
 governor refuses to lower them. All design values (battery capacity, sweep
 rate, obstacle-avoidance rate) are modelled-labelled — no measured data
 exists yet. Starlink Direct is the assumed remote-monitoring transport:
 no spectrum of our own, coverage truth external (Starlink coverage map)."
 :itonami.blueprint/operations
 [{:op/name :design/propose
   :op/effect :propose
   :op/note "mechanism configuration proposal (brush count, vacuum path, obstacle-sensing layout)"}
  {:op/name :design/validate
   :op/effect :propose
   :op/note "invariant check: sweep coverage rate per floor area, obstacle-avoidance rate; all values modelled-labelled"}
  {:op/name :safety/gate
   :op/effect :propose
   :op/note "child/pet contact stop conditions, sharp-object stop — permanent structural gate, never absent from any phase's :auto set"}
  {:op/name :sim/run
   :op/effect :propose
   :op/note "virtual cleaning simulation (floor area, obstacles, battery); results are modelled, not measured"}
  {:op/name :bom/observe
   :op/effect :observe
   :op/note "read-only observation of the bill of materials; prices are never proposed (unsettled)"}]
 :itonami.blueprint/boundaries
 {:physical-control "no op drives a real robot; design-only (actuator paths belong to a separate runtime)"
  :robot "cloud-itonami/robot is the general-purpose robot repo; this repo specialises in cleaning-robot design"
  :open-robo "cloud-itonami/open-robo is the OSS robot platform; this repo designs applications on top"
  :starlink "remote monitoring via Starlink Direct wholesale; no spectrum of our own"}}